#!/bin/bash
# Browser performance testing sites

cat << 'EOF'
╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║  Browser GPU/Performance Testing Sites                    ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

▶ GPU Rendering Tests:
  • https://webglsamples.org/aquarium/aquarium.html
    (WebGL aquarium - adjust fish count, watch FPS)

  • https://get.webgl.org/
    (Quick WebGL availability check)

  • https://threejs.org/examples/#webgl_animation_skinning_morph
    (Three.js demos - various 3D scenes)

▶ Video Decode (Hardware Acceleration):
  • YouTube 4K/8K video
    Watch with: chrome://media-internals or about:media
    Look for: "Hardware video decoder"

  • https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LXb3EKWsInQ
    (8K HDR test - should use ~10% CPU if HW decode works)

▶ Comprehensive Benchmarks:
  • https://browserbench.org/Speedometer3.0/
    (Overall browser performance)

  • https://basemark.com/benchmarks/basemark-web/
    (GPU + CPU comprehensive test)

▶ Canvas/Rendering:
  • https://testdrive-archive.azurewebsites.net/performance/fishietank/
    (HTML5 Fish Tank - classic test)

  • https://www.kevs3d.co.uk/dev/phoria/
    (3D rendering demos)

▶ Real-time Validation:
  While testing, monitor in another terminal:

  # Watch GPU usage
  $ radeontop

  # Watch CPU usage (should be LOW with HW accel)
  $ htop

  # Check video decoder
  Chrome: chrome://media-internals
  Firefox: about:media (less detailed)

▶ What to look for:
  ✓ High FPS (60+ for GPU tests)
  ✓ Low CPU usage during video (<15%)
  ✓ GPU usage spike in radeontop during 3D
  ✓ No frame drops or stuttering
  ✓ chrome://gpu shows "Vulkan: Enabled"

EOF
